DeepEP communication-buffer memory per GPU (bytes requested from the allocator)
hidden=7168, top-8, experts=max(256, EP), 8 GPUs per NVLink domain, FP8 dispatch, BF16 combine
MiB = 2^20 B, GiB = 2^30 B. 'only-RDMA (a)' = send/staging bytes the NIC reads as RDMA source;
a load/store fabric stores directly into the peer's receive buffer (as DeepEP does for NVLink peers).

======================================================================================================================
DeepEP V1 low-latency (decode), NVSHMEM IBGDA, 128 tokens/rank (config.hpp:122-188; docs/legacy.md:246-256)
======================================================================================================================
   EP  (a) send/staging   (b) RDMA recv  (c) NVLink side  (d) signal/meta         total  NIC-registered  only-RDMA (a)
    8         910.0 MiB       910.0 MiB          0.0 MiB          0.0 MiB      1.78 GiB        1.78 GiB      910.0 MiB
   16         910.0 MiB       910.0 MiB          0.0 MiB          0.0 MiB      1.78 GiB        1.78 GiB      910.0 MiB
  128         910.0 MiB       910.0 MiB          0.0 MiB          0.0 MiB      1.78 GiB        1.78 GiB      910.0 MiB
  256         910.0 MiB       910.0 MiB          0.0 MiB          0.0 MiB      1.78 GiB        1.78 GiB      910.0 MiB
  512          1.78 GiB        1.78 GiB          0.0 MiB          0.0 MiB      3.55 GiB        3.55 GiB       1.78 GiB
 1024          3.55 GiB        3.55 GiB          0.0 MiB          0.0 MiB      7.11 GiB        7.11 GiB       3.55 GiB
  per-msg bytes: dispatch 14352 B (BF16-sized, config.hpp:143), combine 14560 B (config.hpp:144)
  send buffer (each of 2 odd/even) = max(dispatch_send, combine_send); experts=256:
    dispatch_send = 128 * 14352 = 1,837,056 B; combine_send = 256*128*14560 = 477,102,080 B
  recv buffer (each of 2) = max(dispatch_recv 470,286,336, combine_recv 477,102,080) B
  EP16: 2*send = 954,204,160 B (954.2 MB), 2*recv = 954,204,160 B, signals+pad = 2,176 B, hint = 1,908,410,496 B (1.908 GB); NVSHMEM heap backing (512 MiB chunks) >= 2.00 GiB
  EP256: 2*send = 954,204,160 B (954.2 MB), 2*recv = 954,204,160 B, signals+pad = 2,176 B, hint = 1,908,410,496 B (1.908 GB); NVSHMEM heap backing (512 MiB chunks) >= 2.00 GiB
  EP512: 2*send = 1,908,408,320 B (1908.4 MB), 2*recv = 1,908,408,320 B, signals+pad = 4,224 B, hint = 3,816,820,864 B (3.817 GB); NVSHMEM heap backing (512 MiB chunks) >= 4.00 GiB
  EP1024: 2*send = 3,816,816,640 B (3816.8 MB), 2*recv = 3,816,816,640 B, signals+pad = 8,320 B, hint = 7,633,641,600 B (7.634 GB); NVSHMEM heap backing (512 MiB chunks) >= 7.50 GiB
  experts = 256 for EP<=256 so V1 LL size is independent of EP there; it scales with experts beyond.
  Of (a), 2*dispatch_send = 3,674,112 B is the FP8-cast copy that is also read for NVLink peers (internode_ll.cu:259-270);
  the rest is combine staging used only for non-P2P peers (internode_ll.cu:843-853,910-911).

