DeepEP V1 normal (training/prefill), NVSHMEM, num_sms=24, hint = max(dispatch, combine config) (config.hpp:53-100; legacy.py:233-290; docs/legacy.md:136-147)
======================================================================================================================
  (sizes do not depend on tokens/rank; ring buffers of num_max_*_chunked_recv_tokens per channel)
   EP  (a) send/staging   (b) RDMA recv  (c) NVLink side  (d) signal/meta         total  NIC-registered  only-RDMA (a)
    8           0.0 MiB         0.0 MiB        384.2 MiB          0.0 MiB     384.2 MiB         0.0 MiB        0.0 MiB
   16          52.5 MiB        52.5 MiB        432.2 MiB          0.1 MiB     537.4 MiB       105.2 MiB       52.5 MiB
  128         396.2 MiB       396.2 MiB        840.4 MiB          0.8 MiB      1.60 GiB       793.2 MiB      396.2 MiB
  160         495.2 MiB       495.2 MiB         1.06 GiB          1.0 MiB      2.02 GiB       991.5 MiB      495.2 MiB
  EP16: RDMA hint 110,265,216 B = send half 55,077,120 + recv half 55,077,120 + meta 3,456 + int4 slack 107,520 + pad 0; NVL hint 453,208,704 B; NVSHMEM heap backing >= 512.0 MiB
  EP128: RDMA hint 831,716,352 B = send half 415,438,848 + recv half 415,438,848 + meta 27,648 + int4 slack 811,008 + pad 0; NVL hint 881,247,360 B; NVSHMEM heap backing >= 1.00 GiB
  (a)/(b) per-token terms use kNumMaxTopK=128, kNumMaxScales=128, int64 topk idx (config.hpp:82-83):
  real tokens use far less of each slot, but the allocation is what is pinned/registered.
  V1 normal supports at most 20 nodes (compiled.cuh:6; legacy.py config_map up to 160): EP256+ n/a.
  NVL buffer: cudaMalloc + CUDA IPC (buffer.hpp:132-136), NOT NIC-registered. Workspace 32 MiB cudaMalloc (buffer.hpp:149) not counted.
  with Buffer.num_sms default 20 (legacy.py:31): EP16 total 447.8 MiB, NIC 87.6 MiB, (a) 43.8 MiB; EP128 total 1.33 GiB, NIC 661.0 MiB, (a) 330.2 MiB

